# Generated Artifacts

## Source of Truth

- Do not manually patch generated output. Change the source of truth and
  regenerate; if generation is unavailable, report the blocker instead of
  presenting handwritten output as regenerated.
- Update the generator input, schema, Rust export, build script, or binding
  source first; then regenerate the derived artifact.
- Keep generated Dart bindings, cbindgen headers, exported symbols, and Rust FFI
  signatures aligned.
- Review generated diffs for ABI, layout, naming, and nullability changes before
  accepting them.

## Repository Checks

- The engine build script generates `native/odbc_engine/include/odbc_engine.h`
  from Rust exports and `native/odbc_engine/cbindgen.toml`.
- `tool/ffigen.dart` generates columnar decompression Dart bindings; check the
  affected artifact header for its generator rather than assuming one command
  regenerates every binding.
- Run `dart tool/check_ffi_exports.dart` after export changes and review any
  generated header changes caused by native builds.

## Suppressions

- Generated files may use broader lint suppressions only when allowed by
  `error_handling.mdc`.
- Do not copy generated-file suppressions into handwritten code.

## Build Outputs

- Do not treat `build/`, `target/`, coverage output, temporary generated files,
  or ad-hoc binaries as source files.
- Do not commit regenerated build outputs unless the repository intentionally
  tracks that artifact.
